How to read it: two cameras co-fire when both report motion within 5 minutes of each other. The partner is demonstrably active, so this is not a quiet scene. A camera that has lost part of its detection - motion zones, sensitivity, Smart Alerts, Modes, a schedule, a night setting - shows exactly this signature while still firing on what it does see. Check its motion settings in the Ring app, then walk through its view. This card is rewritten when the flagged set changes, at startup and every 6 h, so recovery progress shown here can be up to 6 h old. The test declines to convict when another partner's co-fires contradict the loss, when the partner fires at more than 2x its usual rate, when the partner has just come back from its own outage, or when the camera's own event rate has not fallen. The flag does NOT clear with time: if the change is deliberate, acknowledge it in cam_motion.py with PARTIAL_LOSS_ACK = {"<camera>": <ack stamp>} (the ack stamp printed above). {{ now().strftime('%b %-d %-I:%M %p') }}.
